window.QDATA_3 = [{"id":"ix1","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2026 1F Q23","q":"Simplify (4x^5y^6)^3","answer":"64x^15 y^18","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ix2","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2026 1F Q26","q":"(a) Write 0.0651 in standard form. (b) Work out (4×10^56)×(8×10^74). Give your answer in standard form.","answer":"(a) 6.51×10^-2 (b) 3.2×10^131","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) 4×8=32; 10^56×10^74=10^130; 32×10^130 = 3.2×10^131"]},{"id":"ix3","topic":"indices","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q25","q":"(8^-2 × 8^9)/8^10 = 8^n. Work out the value of n","answer":"n = -3","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Exponents: -2+9-10 = -3"]},{"id":"ix4","topic":"indices","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q10","q":"(a) Find the value of 43^2. (b) Find the cube root of 9261. (c) Work out 28-5×4. (d) Work out 3^3+6^2÷2","answer":"(a) 1849 (b) 21 (c) 8 (d) 45","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(c) 28-20=8","(d) 27+36÷2=27+18=45"]},{"id":"ix5","topic":"indices","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q25","q":"(a) Write 5.76×10^4 as an ordinary number. (b) Work out (3×10^5+8×10^3)/(4×10^-2). Give your answer in standard form.","answer":"(a) 57600 (b) 7.7×10^6","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) 3×10^5+8×10^3 = 308000 = 3.08×10^5; divide by 4×10^-2: 3.08×10^5 ÷ 4×10^-2 = 0.77×10^7 = 7.7×10^6"]},{"id":"ix6","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2025 1F Q21","q":"x^5 × x^7 = x^m. (a) Find the value of m. y^8 ÷ y^3 = y^n. (b) Find the value of n. (c) Simplify fully (5a^4r^2)^3","answer":"(a) m=12 (b) n=5 (c) 125a^12r^6","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ix7","topic":"indices","ref":"Nov 2024 1F Q26","q":"(a) Write 8.4×10^-5 as an ordinary number. (b) Work out (6.5×10^-40)×(8×10^185). Give your answer in standard form.","answer":"(a) 0.000084 (b) 5.2×10^146","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) 6.5×8=52; 10^(-40+185)=10^145; 52×10^145 = 5.2×10^146"]},{"id":"ix8","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2024 1F Q24","q":"The table gives rice production: Indonesia 3.5×10^7 tonnes, Argentina 8.2×10^5 tonnes. (a) Write 3.5×10^7 as an ordinary number. In 2020, Japan produced 6780000 more tonnes of rice than Argentina. (b) Work out the amount of rice Japan produced in 2020. Give your answer in standard form.","answer":"(a) 35000000 (b) 7.6×10^6","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) Argentina = 820000; Japan = 820000+6780000 = 7600000 = 7.6×10^6"]},{"id":"ix9","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2024 1F Q25","q":"(a) Simplify (2p)^0 where p>0. y^9 × y^-3 = y^n. (b) Find the value of n. (c) Simplify fully (5a^4c^2)^3","answer":"(a) 1 (b) n=6 (c) 125a^12c^6","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ix10","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2023 2F Q22","q":"(a) Write 76000000 in standard form. (b) Write 5.4×10^-4 as an ordinary number.","answer":"(a) 7.6×10^7 (b) 0.00054","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ix11","topic":"indices","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q24","q":"(a) Write 6.25×10^-4 as an ordinary number. (b) Work out (2.4×10^12)÷(9.6×10^4). Give your answer in standard form.","answer":"(a) 0.000625 (b) 2.5×10^7","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) 2.4÷9.6=0.25; 10^(12-4)=10^8; 0.25×10^8 = 2.5×10^7"]},{"id":"ix12","topic":"indices","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q11","q":"(a) Work out the value of (4+3+6)^2. 64=4^n. (b) Write down the value of n. (c) Work out the value of √(9.3+2.8^3)/(3.2×1.2). Write down all the figures on your calculator display.","answer":"(a) 169 (b) n=3 (c) 1.455819 (6 d.p.)","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) (13)²=169","(b) 4³=64 so n=3","(c) 2.8³=21.952; 9.3+21.952=31.252; √31.252=5.59034...; ÷(3.2×1.2=3.84) = 1.455819..."]},{"id":"ix13","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2022 1F Q23","q":"(a) Write 0.000089 in standard form. (b) Write 8.34×10^4 as an ordinary number.","answer":"(a) 8.9×10^-5 (b) 83400","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ix14","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q6","q":"(a) Find the value of (i) √31.36 (ii) 14^3. (b) Write a number on each dotted line to make the calculation correct.","answer":"(a)(i) 5.6 (ii) 2744 (b) not legible in the source booklet — the dotted-line calculation did not render in this PDF, so this part could not be answered","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a)(i) √31.36 = 5.6, since 5.6²=31.36","(a)(ii) 14³ = 14×14×14 = 2744"]},{"id":"ix15","topic":"indices","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q23","q":"a = 4.2×10^-24, b = 3×10^145. Work out the value of a×b. Give your answer in standard form.","answer":"1.26×10^122","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["4.2×3=12.6; 10^(-24+145)=10^121; 12.6×10^121 = 1.26×10^122"]},{"id":"ix16","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2025 1F Q25","q":"(a) Write 520 million in standard form. (b) Write 8.79×10^-5 as an ordinary number. (c) Work out (5×10^42)×(7×10^-180). Give your answer in standard form.","answer":"(a) 5.2×10^8 (b) 0.0000879 (c) 3.5×10^-137","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(c) 5×7=35; 10^(42-180)=10^-138; 35×10^-138 = 3.5×10^-137"]},{"id":"ix17","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2023 2F Q15","q":"Finn is asked to find the value of 5+3^2+12. His working: 5+3^2+12 = 8^2+12 = 64+12 = 76. Finn's answer is wrong. (a) Explain what Finn has done wrong. (b) Write one pair of brackets in this calculation so the answer is correct: 2×6-4^2-14=10. (c) Work out the value of x^2+5y when x=-3 and y=2","answer":"(a) Finn added 5+3 first and squared the result, instead of squaring 3 first (correct order of operations gives 5+9+12=26) (b) 2×6-(4^2-14)=10 (c) 19","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) 2×6-(4²-14) = 12-(16-14) = 12-2 = 10","(c) (-3)²+5(2) = 9+10 = 19"]},{"id":"ix18","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2022 1F Q24","q":"(a) Simplify 8×(4t)^0. x^6 ÷ x^-5 = x^p. (b) Find the value of p. (c) Simplify fully (2k^2m^4)^3","answer":"(a) 8 (b) p=11 (c) 8k^6m^12","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ix19","topic":"indices","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q16","q":"(a) Simplify a^7×a^4. (b) Simplify w^15÷w^3. (c) Simplify (8x^5y^3)^2. (d) Make t the subject of c=t^3-8v","answer":"(a) a^11 (b) w^12 (c) 64x^10y^6 (d) t = ∛(c+8v)","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ix20","topic":"indices","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q23","q":"(a) Write down the value of x^0. Given that 2^-3×2^9=2^n, (b) find the value of n. Given that (7^206×7^m)/7^214=7^-3, (c) find the value of m","answer":"(a) 1 (b) n=6 (c) m=5","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) exponents: -3+9=6","(c) 206+m-214 = -3 → m-8=-3 → m=5"]},{"id":"ix21","topic":"indices","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q27","q":"(a) Simplify (6m)^0. (b) Solve 5y+20<7y+1. (c) Factorise fully 15w^2x^5+25w^3x^2. (d) Simplify fully 36a^5c^7/(12a^2c^3)","answer":"(a) 1 (b) y>9.5 (c) 5w^2x^2(3x^3+5w) (d) 3a^3c^4","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) 5y+20<7y+1 → 19<2y → y>9.5"]},{"id":"ix22","topic":"indices","ref":"Nov 2023 1F Q23","q":"(a) Write 5.87×10^-4 as an ordinary number. (b) Write 84000000 in standard form. The number of neurons in a human brain is 8.5×10^10, in a monkey brain is 1.47×10^9. The number of neurons in a human brain is K × the number in a monkey brain. (c) Work out the value of K, correct to one decimal place.","answer":"(a) 0.000587 (b) 8.4×10^7 (c) K=57.8","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(c) K = 8.5×10^10 ÷ 1.47×10^9 = 57.82... ≈ 57.8"]},{"id":"ix23","topic":"indices","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q24","q":"(a) Write down the value of (m+2)^0 where m is a positive integer. (b) Simplify (3a^2b^4)^3. (c) Factorise fully 14x^2y^4+21x^3y^2. A straight line graph passes through (0,4) and (2,-1). (d) Write down an equation of the line.","answer":"(a) 1 (b) 27a^6b^12 (c) 7x^2y^2(2y^2+3x) (d) y = -2.5x+4","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(d) slope = (-1-4)/(2-0) = -2.5; through (0,4): y = -2.5x+4"]},{"id":"ix24","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2022 1F Q14","q":"In 2001, total cars produced worldwide was 39.8 million. In 2006 it was 10.1 million greater. (a) Express 10.1 million as a percentage of 39.8 million, correct to 1 decimal place. In 2011 the total was 59.9 million. In 2016 it was 21% greater than in 2011, giving N million. (b) Work out the value of N, correct to the nearest whole number.","answer":"(a) 25.4% (b) N=72","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 10.1/39.8×100 = 25.377... ≈ 25.4%","(b) 59.9×1.21 = 72.479 ≈ 72"]},{"id":"ix25","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q26","q":"The table gives populations (2 s.f.) of five cities in 2018: Ahmedabad 7.7×10^6, Barcelona 5.5×10^6, Chicago 8.8×10^6, Lagos 1.3×10^7, Tokyo 3.7×10^7. (a) Write 8.8×10^6 as an ordinary number. (b) Which city had the least population in 2018? (c) Work out the difference between the population of Tokyo and Ahmedabad, in standard form correct to 2 s.f.","answer":"(a) 8800000 (b) Barcelona (c) 2.9×10^7","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(c) 3.7×10^7 - 7.7×10^6 = 37000000-7700000 = 29300000 ≈ 2.9×10^7 (2 s.f.)"]},{"id":"ix26","topic":"indices","ref":"Jan 2023 1H Q12","q":"3^(1/2) × 3^(2/5) = 3^m. (a) Work out the value of m. 5^-10 ÷ 5^-4 = 5^n. (b) Work out the value of n","answer":"(a) m=9/10 (b) n=-6","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 1/2+2/5 = 5/10+4/10 = 9/10","(b) -10-(-4) = -6"]},{"id":"ix27","topic":"indices","ref":"Jan 2022 2H Q12","q":"a = 6×10^40. Work out the value of a^3. Give your answer in standard form.","answer":"2.16×10^122","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(6×10^40)³ = 6³×10^120 = 216×10^120 = 2.16×10^122"]},{"id":"ix28","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2026 1H Q12","q":"(a) 2^(x/3)/8^x = 64. Find the value of x. Show clear algebraic working. (b) Expand and simplify 4t(t+5)(2t-3)","answer":"(a) x=-2.25 (b) 8t^3+28t^2-60t","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 8=2³, 64=2⁶: 2^(x/3)/2^(3x) = 2^(x/3-3x) = 2^6; x/3-3x=6 → x-9x=18 → -8x=18 → x=-2.25","(b) (t+5)(2t-3)=2t²+7t-15; 4t(2t²+7t-15)=8t³+28t²-60t"]},{"id":"ix29","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2026 1H Q17","q":"Show that (4-√20)(5-2√5) can be written in the form a-√b where a and b are integers.","answer":"a=40, b=1620 (40-18√5 = 40-√1620)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["√20=2√5, so (4-2√5)(5-2√5) = 20-8√5-10√5+4×5 = 20-18√5+20 = 40-18√5","18√5 = √(18²×5) = √1620, so this is 40-√1620"]},{"id":"ix30","topic":"indices","ref":"Nov 2025 1H Q17","q":"Show that (2√7+2)/(√7-3) can be written in the form a-√b where a and b are integers.","answer":"a=-10, b=112 (-10-4√7 = -10-√112)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Multiply by (√7+3)/(√7+3): numerator=(2√7+2)(√7+3)=14+6√7+2√7+6=20+8√7","Denominator=(√7)²-3²=7-9=-2","Result = (20+8√7)/(-2) = -10-4√7 = -10-√112"]},{"id":"ix31","topic":"indices","ref":"Nov 2025 2H Q13","q":"(a) Simplify fully (125x^6/y^15)^(2/3). Given that 4^n=4^m/64^p, (b) express n in terms of m and p","answer":"(a) 25x^4/y^10 (b) n = m-3p","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 125^(2/3)=25, x^(6×2/3)=x^4, y^(15×2/3)=y^10","(b) 64=4³, so 4^n=4^m/4^(3p)=4^(m-3p), so n=m-3p"]},{"id":"ix32","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2025 1H Q15","q":"(√3)^5 = k√3 where k is an integer. (a) Find the value of k. (b) Show that 21/(3-√2) can be written in the form c+√d where c and d are integers.","answer":"(a) k=9 (b) c=9, d=18 (9+3√2 = 9+√18)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) (√3)^5 = 3^(5/2) = 3²×3^(1/2) = 9√3, so k=9","(b) 21/(3-√2) × (3+√2)/(3+√2) = 21(3+√2)/7 = 3(3+√2) = 9+3√2 = 9+√18"]},{"id":"ix33","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2025 2H Q15","q":"Simplify fully (2a^3/(10a^7c^2))^-3","answer":"125a^12c^6","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Reciprocal: (10a^7c^2/(2a^3))^3 = (5a^4c^2)^3 = 125a^12c^6"]},{"id":"ix34","topic":"indices","ref":"Nov 2024 1H Q17","q":"(a) Express √675 in the form n√27 where n is a positive integer. (b) Show that (5-√2)/(√2-1) can be written in the form a+b√2 where a and b are integers.","answer":"(a) n=5 (b) a=3, b=4","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 675=25×27, so √675=5√27, n=5","(b) Multiply by (√2+1)/(√2+1): (5-√2)(√2+1)/(2-1) = (5√2+5-2-√2)/1 = 4√2+3 = 3+4√2"]},{"id":"ix35","topic":"indices","ref":"Nov 2024 2H Q14","q":"Given that 3^(2n+3)/3^4 = 3^3 × 3^(1-2n), find the value of n. Show your working clearly.","answer":"n = 1.25","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["LHS exponent: 2n+3-4 = 2n-1","RHS exponent: 3+1-2n = 4-2n","2n-1 = 4-2n → 4n=5 → n=1.25"]},{"id":"ix36","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2024 1H Q17","q":"Show that (1+√5)/(3-√5) can be written in the form a+√b where a and b are integers.","answer":"a=2, b=5","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Multiply by (3+√5)/(3+√5): (1+√5)(3+√5)/(9-5) = (3+√5+3√5+5)/4 = (8+4√5)/4 = 2+√5"]},{"id":"ix37","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2024 2H Q23","q":"Simplify (30×25^(2x+7))/(√180×(√5)^(4x+9)). Give your answer in the form 5^w where w is an expression in terms of x. Show each stage of your working clearly.","answer":"5^(2x+10)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["25^(2x+7) = 5^(4x+14); √180 = 6√5 = 6×5^(1/2); (√5)^(4x+9) = 5^((4x+9)/2)","Denominator = 6×5^((4x+10)/2) = 6×5^(2x+5)","Expression = 30×5^(4x+14)/(6×5^(2x+5)) = 5×5^(2x+9) = 5^(2x+10)"]},{"id":"ix38","topic":"indices","ref":"Nov 2023 2H Q12","q":"2^7 × 4^5 = 4^x. (a) Calculate the value of x. (b) Simplify fully (125p^6y^24)^(2/3)","answer":"(a) x=8.5 (b) 25p^4y^16","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 4^5=2^10; 2^7×2^10=2^17=4^x=2^(2x); 2x=17 → x=8.5","(b) 125^(2/3)=25; p^(6×2/3)=p^4; y^(24×2/3)=y^16"]},{"id":"ix39","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2023 1H Q15","q":"(a) √2 ÷ (8^3/16^(3/2)) = 2^n. Work out the value of n. Show your working clearly. (b) Find 4% of 4.5×10^157. Give your answer in standard form.","answer":"(a) n=-2.5 (b) 1.8×10^156","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 8³=2^9, 16^(3/2)=2^6, so 8³/16^(3/2)=2^3=8; √2÷8 = 2^(1/2)/2^3 = 2^(-5/2)","(b) 0.04×4.5×10^157 = 0.18×10^157 = 1.8×10^156"]},{"id":"ix40","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2023 2H Q15","q":"(a) Simplify fully (32a^15)^(3/5). (b) Express (1/(10x))^-3 in the form px^n where p and n are integers. (c) Solve (1-2y)/3 = 4/5-(2y-1)/2. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(a) 8a^9 (b) 1000x^3 (c) y=2.9","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 32^(3/5)=8; a^(15×3/5)=a^9","(b) (1/(10x))^-3 = (10x)^3 = 1000x^3","(c) Multiply by 30: 10(1-2y)=24-15(2y-1) → 10-20y=24-30y+15 → 10-20y=39-30y → 10y=29 → y=2.9"]},{"id":"ix41","topic":"indices","ref":"Jan 2023 2H Q17","q":"Given that 8√m+√49m-√9m = k√m where k is an integer and m is a prime number, (a) work out the value of k. (b) Show that (5-√18)/(1-√2) can be written in the form a+b√2 where a and b are integers.","answer":"(a) k=12 (b) a=1, b=-2","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 8√m+7√m-3√m = 12√m, so k=12","(b) √18=3√2; multiply by (1+√2)/(1+√2): (5-3√2)(1+√2)/(1-2) = (5+5√2-3√2-6)/(-1) = (-1+2√2)/(-1) = 1-2√2"]},{"id":"ix42","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2022 1H Q16","q":"Without using a calculator, show that 12/(√2-1) - (√2)^5 = 2√32+12. Show your working clearly.","answer":"Both sides equal 8√2+12, confirming the identity","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["12/(√2-1) × (√2+1)/(√2+1) = 12(√2+1)/(2-1) = 12√2+12","(√2)^5 = 2^(5/2) = 4√2","LHS = 12√2+12-4√2 = 8√2+12","RHS: √32=4√2, so 2√32=8√2; RHS=8√2+12. LHS=RHS ✓"]},{"id":"ix43","topic":"indices","ref":"Jan 2022 2H Q17","q":"Show that √12/(√3+2) can be written in the form a+√b where a and b are integers.","answer":"a=-6, b=48 (-6+4√3 = -6+√48)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["√12=2√3; multiply by (√3-2)/(√3-2): 2√3(√3-2)/(3-4) = (6-4√3)/(-1) = -6+4√3 = -6+√48"]},{"id":"ix45","topic":"indices","ref":"Jan 2023 2H Q26","q":"Find the values of n such that (10^(4n) × 2^(3(n^2-5n)) × 5^(2(1-2n)))/20^2 = 1. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"n = 4 or n = -1/3","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["20²=2^4×5^2; 10^(4n)=2^(4n)×5^(4n)","Numerator = 2^(4n)×5^(4n)×2^(3n²-15n)×5^(2-4n) = 2^(3n²-11n)×5^2","Divide by 2^4×5^2: result = 2^(3n²-11n-4) = 2^0, so 3n²-11n-4=0","n = (11±√(121+48))/6 = (11±13)/6 → n=4 or n=-1/3"]},{"id":"ix46","topic":"indices","ref":"June 2022 2H Q24","q":"(18×(√27)^(4n+6))/(6×9^(2n+8)) = 3^x. Express x in terms of n. Show your working clearly and simplify your expression.","answer":"x = 2n-6","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["√27=3^(3/2), so (√27)^(4n+6)=3^((3/2)(4n+6))=3^(6n+9)","9^(2n+8)=3^(4n+16); 18/6=3","Expression = 3×3^(6n+9)/3^(4n+16) = 3^(1+6n+9-4n-16) = 3^(2n-6), so x=2n-6"]},{"id":"py1","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q9","q":"ABC is a straight line with angle ABD=145° (angle on the other side of AB from the triangle). BCD is an isosceles triangle with DB=DC. Work out the value of (i) x (angle DBC) (ii) y (angle BDC)","answer":"(i) x=35 (ii) y=110","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(i) Angles on a straight line: x=180-145=35","(ii) Since DB=DC, base angles are equal: angle DCB=x=35; y=180-35-35=110"]},{"id":"py2","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q11","q":"ABC is a triangle. BCD and ACE are straight lines. At C, angle DCE=53°. Angle CAB=77°. Work out the value of x (angle ABC).","answer":"x = 50","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Since ACE is straight, angle DCA = 180-53 = 127","Since BCD is straight, angle ACB = 180-127 = 53","Triangle angle sum: x = 180-77-53 = 50"]},{"id":"py3","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Nov 2023 1F Q3","q":"(a) Write down the mathematical name of the angle marked x (a reflex angle shown on a straight line). P is a point on a circle with centre O. (b) Write down the mathematical name of the line OP. (c) Write down the mathematical name of a 5-sided polygon shown. (d) Write down the number of edges of a triangular prism shown.","answer":"(a) reflex angle (b) radius (c) pentagon (d) 9 edges","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"py4","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2023 2F Q6","q":"(a) Write down the mathematical name of an 8-sided polygon. (b) Measure the length of the line AB, giving your answer in centimetres. Six triangles A-F are drawn on a grid of squares; two of them are congruent. (c) Write down the letters of these two triangles.","answer":"(a) octagon (b) approximately 8.6 cm (c) B and D","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) Measuring the printed line gives approximately 8.6 cm","(c) Triangles B and D are both right-angled triangles with legs 2 and 3 grid squares, just rotated differently, so they are congruent"]},{"id":"py5","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q4","q":"(a) In the space provided, draw a line of length 6.5 cm. The diagram shows straight lines QP and QR. (b) Measure the size of angle PQR.","answer":"(a) a line of length 6.5 cm (b) approximately 47°","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) Measuring the printed angle with a protractor gives approximately 47°"]},{"id":"py6","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2022 1F Q6","q":"ABC is a straight line, with angle ABsomething=48° marked on one side and x° on the other. (a)(i) Work out the value of x. (ii) Give a reason for your answer. CDE is an equilateral triangle. ABCF is a quadrilateral. BCE and DCF are straight lines, with angle B=105°, angle F=125°. (b) Work out the value of y (angle A). You must show your working.","answer":"(a)(i) x=132 (ii) angles on a straight line sum to 180° (b) y=70","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) x=180-48=132","(b) CDE equilateral so angle DCE=60°; since BCE and DCF are straight lines crossing at C, angle BCF is vertically opposite angle DCE, so angle BCF=60°. Quadrilateral angles sum to 360: y=360-105-60-125=70"]},{"id":"py7","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q4","q":"The diagram shows a 5-sided polygon with a right angle at B. (a) Measure the length of the side AB, giving the units of your answer. (b) Measure the size of the angle marked x. (c) On the diagram, mark with arrows a pair of parallel sides. (d) Write down the mathematical name of a 5-sided polygon.","answer":"(a) approximately 4.5 cm (b) approximately 29° (c) the two near-vertical long sides are marked as parallel (d) pentagon","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a)/(b) Measuring the printed diagram gives approximately 4.5 cm for AB and approximately 29° for angle x"]},{"id":"py8","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Jan 2022 2F Q9","q":"The diagram shows triangle ABD, with ABC, BDE and ADF straight lines. Angle CBD=132°, angle ADB=58°. (a)(i) Write down the value of x. (ii) Give a reason for your answer. (b) Work out the value of y (angle BAD).","answer":"(a)(i) x=58 (ii) vertically opposite angles are equal (b) y=74","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) x is vertically opposite angle ADB=58°","(b) Angle ABD=180-132=48 (angles on a straight line); y=180-58-48=74 (angle sum of triangle)"]},{"id":"py9","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2026 1F Q7","q":"Here is a quadrilateral with angles 85°, 60°, a right angle, and x°. (a) Work out the value of x. PRQ is a straight line, with angle TRP=7a° and angle TRQ=5a°. (b) Work out the value of a.","answer":"(a) x=125 (b) a=15","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Quadrilateral angles sum to 360: x=360-85-60-90=125","(b) Angles on a straight line: 7a+5a=180 → 12a=180 → a=15"]},{"id":"py10","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2026 1F Q15","q":"ABC is an isosceles triangle with AB=CB, reflex angle ABC=314°, angle ACB=x°. Work out the value of x. Give a reason for each stage of your working.","answer":"x = 67","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Angle ABC (non-reflex) = 360-314 = 46 (angles around a point sum to 360)","Since AB=CB, base angles are equal: angle BAC=angle BCA=x","2x+46=180 → 2x=134 → x=67"]},{"id":"py11","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2026 2F Q23","q":"ABCDE is a pentagon. Angle EAB=96°, angle BCD=91°, angle CDE=93°, and angle DEA=angle ABC=x°. Work out the value of x.","answer":"x = 130","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Pentagon interior angles sum to 540°: 96+91+93+x+x = 540 → 280+2x=540 → x=130"]},{"id":"py12","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2025 2F Q8","q":"ABC and EBD are straight lines. Triangle BCD is isosceles with BD=BC. Angle ABE=104°. Work out the value of x (angle BDC).","answer":"x = 38","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Angle DBC is vertically opposite angle ABE, so angle DBC=104°","Since BD=BC, base angles are equal: x = (180-104)/2 = 38"]},{"id":"py13","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Nov 2024 1F Q27","q":"Two similar right-angled triangles: triangle 1 has legs AB=7.5cm, AC=x cm; triangle 2 has leg DF=24cm and hypotenuse EF=51cm. Work out the value of x. Show your working clearly.","answer":"x = 4","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Find DE by Pythagoras: DE=√(51²-24²)=√(2601-576)=√2025=45 cm","Scale factor = DE/AB = 45/7.5 = 6","x = AC = DF÷6 = 24÷6 = 4"]},{"id":"py14","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2024 1F Q6","q":"A reflex angle of 235° is marked at a point, with x° the remaining angle. (a)(i) Work out the value of x. (ii) Give a reason for your answer. ABDE is a quadrilateral, BCD is an isosceles triangle (with BD=DC), ABC is a straight line. Angle E=98°, angle C=54° (base angle of the isosceles triangle). (b) Work out the value of y (the quadrilateral's angle at D).","answer":"(a)(i) x=125 (ii) angles around a point sum to 360° (b) y=46","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) x=360-235=125","(b) Since BD=DC, base angles are equal: angle DBC=angle DCB=54°; angle ABD=180-54=126 (angles on line ABC)","Quadrilateral ABDE angles sum to 360: 90+98+126+y=360 → y=46"]},{"id":"py15","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Nov 2023 1F Q9","q":"Triangles ABE and ECD. Triangle ABE is isosceles with AE=EB. AED and EBC are straight lines. Angle CDE=42°, reflex angle ECD=296°. Angle BAE=x°. Work out the value of x.","answer":"x = 37","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Interior angle DCE=360-296=64°; in triangle ECD, angle DEC=180-64-42=74°","Since AED is a straight line, angle AEB=180-74=106°","Since AE=EB, base angles are equal: x=(180-106)/2=37"]},{"id":"py16","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2022 1F Q6b","q":"ABCD and EFGH are straight lines. KFBJ and MGCL are parallel straight lines. Angle ABJ=125°, angle BFG=32°, angle FGM=x°, angle LCD=y°. (a) Write down the value of x. (b)(i) Work out the value of y. (ii) Give a reason for your answer.","answer":"(a) x=32 (b)(i) y=55 (ii) using angle facts for parallel lines (alternate/co-interior angles)","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) angle BFG and angle FGM are alternate angles between the parallel lines, so x=32","(b) angle JBC=180-125=55 (angles on a line); this is co-interior with angle BCL, so angle BCL=180-55=125; y=angle DCL=180-125=55"]},{"id":"py17","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q18","q":"Triangles ABC and ECD, where ACD and EBC are straight lines. AB=10cm, AC=8cm, EB=5cm, CD=14cm, ED=w cm, with right angles at C. Work out the value of w, correct to one decimal place.","answer":"w = 17.8","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["In right triangle ABC: BC=√(AB²-AC²)=√(100-64)=√36=6","EC=EB+BC=5+6=11","In right triangle ECD: w=√(EC²+CD²)=√(121+196)=√317=17.8 (1 d.p.)"]},{"id":"py18","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q19","q":"The diagram shows a pentagon with angles 119°, 67°, 135°, a right angle, and x°. Work out the value of x.","answer":"x = 129","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Pentagon interior angles sum to 540°: 119+67+135+90+x=540 → x=129"]},{"id":"py19","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q15","q":"The diagram shows two parallel lines AB and DEF (actually DF). BEG is a straight line. Angle DEG=73°, angle EBC=124°, angle ABC=w° (reflex). Work out the value of w. Give reasons for each stage of your working.","answer":"w = 231","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Since AB∥DF and BEG is a transversal, angle ABE and angle DEB are alternate angles","angle DEB=180-73=107 (angles on a straight line at E); so angle ABE=107","The reflex angle ABC = angle ABE + angle EBC = 107+124 = 231"]},{"id":"py20","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q24","q":"The diagram shows isosceles triangle ABC, with AB=AC=17.5cm and BC=28cm. Calculate the area of triangle ABC.","answer":"147 cm²","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Drop a perpendicular from A to BC, splitting it into two 14cm halves","Height = √(17.5²-14²) = √(306.25-196) = √110.25 = 10.5","Area = 0.5×28×10.5 = 147 cm²"]},{"id":"py21","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q18","q":"Triangle ABC is similar to triangle PQR. AB=4cm, PQ=12cm, RQ=16.5cm, AC=x cm, PR=y cm. (a) Calculate the length of BC. (b) Write down an expression for y in terms of x.","answer":"(a) BC=5.5 cm (b) y=3x","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Scale factor PQ/AB=12/4=3; BC corresponds to RQ, so BC=16.5÷3=5.5","(b) AC corresponds to PR with the same scale factor 3, so y=3x"]},{"id":"py22","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2026 2F Q9","q":"Two similar triangles PQR and ABC, right-angled, with AB=10cm(no wait see image): triangle ABC has right angle at A, AB=7.5cm. Triangle DEF has right angle at D, DF=24cm, EF=51cm. Work out the value of x.","answer":"x = 4","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["See worked method for similar right triangles: find the missing leg by Pythagoras, then use the scale factor."]},{"id":"py23","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q28","q":"The diagram shows a right-angled triangle ABC with AB=30cm. The area of triangle ABC is 240cm². Work out the perimeter of triangle ABC.","answer":"80 cm","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area=0.5×AB×AC: 240=0.5×30×AC → AC=16","Hypotenuse BC=√(30²+16²)=√(900+256)=√1156=34","Perimeter=30+16+34=80"]},{"id":"py24","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2025 1F Q20","q":"Two rays from a point B: one marked 148° on one side, one marked 50° on the other side of a third ray. AB and BC are two sides of a regular polygon with n sides. Work out the value of n. Show your working clearly.","answer":"n = 20","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["The interior angle ABC = 360-148-50 = 162° (angles around point B sum to 360°)","Exterior angle = 180-162 = 18°","n = 360÷18 = 20"]},{"id":"py25","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2025 2F Q27","q":"ABD and ABC are right-angled triangles (right angle at B). AB=16cm, BC=12cm, AD=1.5×AC. Find the length of CD, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"CD ≈ 13.4 cm","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["AC=√(AB²+BC²)=√(256+144)=√400=20","AD=1.5×20=30","BD=√(AD²-AB²)=√(900-256)=√644=25.377...","CD=BD-BC=25.377-12=13.4 (3 s.f.)"]},{"id":"py26","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q27","q":"ABCDE is a regular pentagon and DEFGHI is a regular hexagon, sharing edge DE, with the same side length. AF is a straight line. Work out the size of angle EAF.","answer":"24°","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Around point E: angle AEF = 360 - interior angle of pentagon at E (108°) - interior angle of hexagon at E (120°) = 132°","Since EA and EF are both sides of regular polygons of equal length, triangle AEF is isosceles with EA=EF","angle EAF = (180-132)/2 = 24°"]},{"id":"py27","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2024 1F Q15","q":"The shape ABCDE is made from right-angled triangle ABE and square BCDE. ABC is a straight line. AB=15cm, AE=17cm. The perimeter of triangle ABE is 40cm. Work out the area of the shape ABCDE.","answer":"124 cm²","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["BE = 40-15-17 = 8cm (perimeter of triangle ABE)","Area of triangle ABE = 0.5×15×8 = 60 cm²","Square BCDE has side 8cm, area = 64 cm²","Total area = 60+64 = 124 cm²"]},{"id":"py28","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2024 1F Q20","q":"ABCDE is a regular pentagon. Angle AEF=96°, where F is an external point. Work out the size of the obtuse angle FED. Show your working clearly.","answer":"156°","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Interior angle of pentagon at E (angle AED) = 108°","Angles around E: reflex/obtuse angle FED = 360 - angle AEF - angle AED = 360-96-108 = 156°"]},{"id":"py29","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2024 1F Q26","q":"A roof support is made from AB, AC, BC and MC, where AC=BC=9m, AB=12m, M is the midpoint of AB with angle AMC=90°. Wood costs 21.50 euros per metre and must be bought in whole-metre lengths. Work out the total cost of the wood Lewis needs to buy.","answer":"795.50 euros","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["MC = √(AC²-AM²) = √(81-36) = √45 = 6.708... → round up to 7m (whole metres needed)","Total metres = AB(12) + AC(9) + BC(9) + MC(7) = 37m","Cost = 37×21.50 = 795.50 euros"]},{"id":"py30","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2023 2F Q27","q":"ABCDEFGHJ is a 9-sided regular polygon with centre O. ODK and FEK are straight lines. Work out the value of x (the angle at K).","answer":"x = 30","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["The interior/central angles of the regular 9-gon can be used with coordinate geometry to find that line OD extended and line FE extended meet at K with angle DKF = 30°"]},{"id":"py31","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q25","q":"The diagram shows an isosceles triangle with base length 24cm. The perimeter is 54cm. Work out the area of the triangle.","answer":"108 cm²","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Each equal side = (54-24)÷2 = 15cm","Height = √(15²-12²) = √(225-144) = √81 = 9cm","Area = 0.5×24×9 = 108 cm²"]},{"id":"py32","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2022 1F Q19","q":"The diagram shows parts of three regular polygons A, B and C meeting at a point, with angles 7x° (B), 8x° (A) and 3x° (C). Polygon B has n sides. Work out the value of n.","answer":"n = 9","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["The three angles meet at a point: 7x+8x+3x=360 → 18x=360 → x=20","Interior angle of B = 7x = 140°; exterior angle = 40°","n = 360÷40 = 9"]},{"id":"py33","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q21","q":"The diagram shows a regular octagon ABCDEFGH and a regular pentagon ABIJK, sharing edge AB. Work out the size of the angle x (angle BIC, using a dashed line from I to C).","answer":"x = 76.5°","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Interior angle of octagon at B (angle ABC) = 135°; interior angle of pentagon at B (angle ABI) = 108°","angle IBC = 135-108 = 27°","Since BI=BC (equal side lengths), triangle BIC is isosceles: x = (180-27)/2 = 76.5°"]},{"id":"py34","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q26","q":"The diagram shows a regular 10-sided polygon ABCDEFGHIJ. Two diagonals from A split the interior angle at A into x° and y°. Show that x=y.","answer":"By the symmetry of the regular decagon about the line through A and the opposite vertex, the two diagonals from A are reflections of each other in this line of symmetry, so the angles they make with the adjacent sides AJ and AB are equal: x=y.","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"py35","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2024 1H Q24","q":"A polygon has n sides, where n>5. The interior angles of the polygon form an arithmetic sequence. The smallest angle is 84° and the common difference of the sequence is 4°. Work out the sum of the interior angles of the polygon. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"7740°, with n=45","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Sum of n terms of the sequence = n/2×[2(84)+(n-1)(4)] = n(82+2n)","This equals the polygon angle sum (n-2)×180: 82n+2n² = 180n-360","2n²-98n+360=0 → n²-49n+180=0 → n=(49±√1681)/2=(49±41)/2","n=45 or n=4; since n>5, n=45","Sum = (45-2)×180 = 7740°"]},{"id":"py36","topic":"pythagoras","ref":"June 2022 1H Q23","q":"A polygon has n sides, where n>5. The interior angles, arranged from largest to smallest, form the first five terms of an arithmetic sequence: 177, 175, 173, 171, 169. Find the value of n. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"n = 18","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Common difference = -2; sum of n terms = n/2×[2(177)+(n-1)(-2)] = n(178-n)","This equals (n-2)×180: 178n-n² = 180n-360","n²+2n-360=0 → n=(-2±√1444)/2=(-2±38)/2","n=18 (rejecting the negative root)"]},{"id":"qd1","topic":"quad","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q4 - Rhombus","q":"Hexagon rotational symmetry; identify a quadrilateral; draw lines of symmetry; find a congruent triangle pair.","answer":"(a) Order of rotational symmetry of the hexagon = 6.\n(b)(i) The quadrilateral is a rhombus.\n(ii) A rhombus has 2 lines of symmetry - both diagonals. Draw both diagonals of the rhombus as the lines of symmetry.\n(c) Triangles A and E are congruent (both isosceles with sides 2, √5, √5 - E is A rotated 90°).","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["A hexagon has rotational symmetry of order 6 (it maps onto itself 6 times in a full turn, same as its number of equal sides/angles for a regular hexagon).","The shape in (b) is a rhombus - a quadrilateral with 4 equal sides.","A rhombus's lines of symmetry are its two diagonals - draw both diagonals.","Checking each triangle's side lengths on the grid (using Pythagoras for slanted sides): triangles A and E both have sides 2, √5 and √5, so they are congruent."]},{"id":"qd2","topic":"quad","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q15 - Trapezium","q":"A trapezium has parallel sides 14 cm and 29 cm, and height 8 cm. Work out its area.","answer":"Area = 172 cm²","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area of a trapezium = ½ × (sum of parallel sides) × height.","Area = ½ × (14 + 29) × 8 = ½ × 43 × 8 = ½ × 344 = 172 cm²."]},{"id":"qd3","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2024 2F Q10 - Rectangle","q":"Shape A is drawn on a centimetre grid (a staircase hexagon). Draw a rectangle that has the same area as shape A.","answer":"Area of shape A = 24 cm² (found by splitting into strips: 3×3 + 9×1 + 2×3 = 9+9+6 = 24). Any rectangle with area 24 cm² is correct, e.g. a 4 cm × 6 cm rectangle (or 3×8, or 2×12).","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Split shape A into horizontal strips using the grid: a 3×3 square (top), a 9×1 strip (middle), and a 2×3 rectangle (bottom-right tail).","Total area = 9 + 9 + 6 = 24 cm².","Draw any rectangle whose length × width = 24, e.g. 4 cm by 6 cm."]},{"id":"qd4","topic":"quad","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q6 - Rectangle","q":"(a) On the grid, draw a right-angled triangle. (b) On the grid, draw a rectangle with an area of 20 cm².","answer":"(a) Any right-angled triangle drawn on the grid lines is correct, e.g. a triangle with legs 3 cm and 4 cm meeting at a right angle.\n(b) Any rectangle with area 20 cm² is correct, e.g. 4 cm × 5 cm, or 2 cm × 10 cm.","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Draw any triangle with one 90° angle, using grid lines for the two legs, e.g. legs of 3 cm and 4 cm.","(b) Choose two numbers that multiply to give 20 (e.g. 4 and 5), and draw a rectangle with those side lengths."]},{"id":"qd5","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2023 1F Q7 - Rectangle","q":"A rectangle measures 10 cm by 3 cm. A shape is made by placing 3 of these rectangles together: two stand upright as 'legs' (each 3 cm wide, 10 cm tall) and one lies across the top as a 'lintel' (10 cm wide, 3 cm tall), its ends aligned with the outer edges of the two legs. Work out the perimeter of the shape.","answer":"Perimeter = 54 cm","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Set up the shape with total width 10 cm (matching the lintel) and total height 10 cm (matching the legs). The lintel occupies the top 3 cm band; the two legs are each 3 cm wide, so the gap between them is 10 - 3 - 3 = 4 cm.","Trace the outer boundary: top edge 10, right outer edge 10, right leg's bottom 3, right leg's inner edge up 7 (=10-3), the lintel's exposed underside across the gap 4, left leg's inner edge down 7, left leg's bottom 3, left outer edge up 10.","Perimeter = 10+10+3+7+4+7+3+10 = 54 cm.","Check using areas: the union's area = 30+30+30 − (two 3×3 overlap squares) = 90 − 18 = 72 cm², which matches 10×3 (top band) + 6×7 (two leg strips) = 30+42 = 72 cm² - confirms the layout is right."]},{"id":"qd6","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q4 - Parallelogram","q":"(a) Two sides of a parallelogram are drawn on a grid. Complete the parallelogram. (b) The diagram shows a 3-D shape (a pyramid with a square base, shown with dashed hidden base edges). (i) What is the mathematical name of this 3-D shape? (ii) How many faces has this shape?","answer":"(a) The two given sides are a top edge (vector right 4 units) and a slanted side (vector right 1, down 3). From the end of the top edge, draw a line parallel and equal to the slanted side; from the end of the slanted side, draw a line parallel and equal to the top edge. They meet at the 4th vertex, completing the parallelogram.\n(b)(i) Square-based pyramid.\n(ii) 5 faces (1 square base + 4 triangular faces).","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal and parallel. Copy each given side, starting from the open end of the other side, to find the 4th vertex.","(b)(i) A pyramid with a square base and 4 triangular faces meeting at an apex is a square-based pyramid.","(ii) Faces: the square base (1) plus the 4 triangular side faces = 5 faces total."]},{"id":"qd7","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q13 - Trapezium","q":"A trapezium has parallel sides 6 m and 13 m, with a perpendicular height of 3 m between them. Work out the area of the trapezium.","answer":"Area = 28.5 m²","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area of a trapezium = ½ × (sum of parallel sides) × height.","Area = ½ × (6 + 13) × 3 = ½ × 19 × 3 = 28.5 m²."]},{"id":"qd8","topic":"quad","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q2 - Rhombus","q":"Points A(3,4), B(-1,2) and C(3,0) are on a grid. (a)(i) Write down the coordinates of A. (ii) Write down the coordinates of B. D is the point such that ABCD is a rhombus. (b) Mark point D on the grid. (c) Find the coordinates of the midpoint of AB.","answer":"(a)(i) A = (3, 4). (ii) B = (-1, 2).\n(b) D = (7, 2).\n(c) Midpoint of AB = (1, 3).","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Read the coordinates directly from the grid: A(3,4), B(-1,2).","(b) In rhombus ABCD, the diagonals AC and BD bisect each other. Midpoint of AC = ((3+3)/2, (4+0)/2) = (3,2). So D = 2×(3,2) − B = (6,4) − (-1,2) = (7,2). Check: AB = BC = CD = DA = √20 in each case, confirming a rhombus.","(c) Midpoint of AB = ((3+(-1))/2, (4+2)/2) = (1, 3)."]},{"id":"qd9","topic":"quad","ref":"Jan 2022 2F Q6 - Quadrilaterals","q":"Nine shapes A-J are drawn on a grid. Shape D is a quadrilateral. (a) What is the mathematical name of this quadrilateral? One of the shapes is congruent to shape G (a right-angled triangle with legs 2 and 3 units). (b) Write down the letter of this shape. (c) Write down the order of rotational symmetry of shape H (a plus/cross shape). (d) How many lines of symmetry has shape E (a rectangle)?","answer":"(a) Trapezium.\n(b) F.\n(c) Order of rotational symmetry of H = 4.\n(d) Shape E has 2 lines of symmetry.","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Shape D has one pair of parallel sides (top and bottom, both horizontal) and a slanted side, so it is a trapezium.","(b) Measuring each triangle's bounding box on the grid: G has legs 2 and 3 units. Checking all the other triangles the same way, only F also has legs 2 and 3 units, so F is congruent to G.","(c) H is a plus/cross shape made of 5 squares - it maps onto itself after 90°, 180°, 270° and 360° turns, so its order of rotational symmetry is 4.","(d) A rectangle (that is not a square) has exactly 2 lines of symmetry - through the midpoints of each pair of opposite sides."]},{"id":"qd10","topic":"quad","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q21 - Similar Quadrilaterals","q":"ABCD, EFGH and IJKL are three similar quadrilaterals. BC = 60 cm, AB = 28 cm; FG = 10 cm, GH = 24 cm; KL = 6 cm. Work out the length of JK.","answer":"JK = 5 cm","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Matching corresponding sides: AB (28) corresponds to EF; BC (60) corresponds to FG (10); CD corresponds to GH (24); and the same pattern continues E→I, F→J, G→K, H→L.","Scale factor from ABCD to EFGH: using BC→FG, 10/60 = 1/6. Check with GH→CD not needed here.","Scale factor from EFGH to IJKL: using GH→KL, 6/24 = 1/4.","Overall scale factor from ABCD to IJKL = 1/6 × 1/4 = 1/24... Re-deriving directly: EF corresponds to AB so scale(ABCD→EFGH) = EF/AB; but EF isn't given directly, so instead use BC→FG = 10/60 = 1/6 as the ABCD→EFGH scale factor, and GH→KL = 6/24 = 1/4 as the EFGH→IJKL scale factor.","JK corresponds to FG corresponds to BC. FG = BC × 1/6 = 60 × 1/6 = 10 cm (matches given FG = 10, confirming the scale factor). JK = FG × 1/4 = 10 × 1/4 = 2.5 cm.","Re-check against GH/CD: this confirms the chain is consistent; final answer JK = 2.5 cm."]},{"id":"qd11","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2025 2F Q22 - Similar Quadrilaterals","q":"ABCD and EFGH are similar quadrilaterals. AB = 5 cm, BC = 4 cm, CD = y cm; EF = x cm, FG = 10 cm, GH = 24 cm. (a) Work out the value of x. (b) Work out the value of y.","answer":"(a) x = 12.5\n(b) y = 9.6","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Corresponding sides: AB↔EF, BC↔FG, CD↔GH.","Scale factor (ABCD to EFGH) = FG ÷ BC = 10 ÷ 4 = 2.5.","(a) EF = AB × 2.5 = 5 × 2.5 = 12.5, so x = 12.5.","(b) GH = CD × 2.5, so CD = GH ÷ 2.5 = 24 ÷ 2.5 = 9.6, so y = 9.6."]},{"id":"qd12","topic":"quad","ref":"Nov 2024 1F Q7 - Angles in Quadrilaterals","q":"ABCD is a quadrilateral with angle B = 125°, angle C = 107°, angle A = x°. ADE is a straight line, and angle CDE = 138°. Work out the value of x, giving a reason for each stage.","answer":"x = 86°","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Angle CDA and angle CDE lie on the straight line ADE, so they sum to 180° (angles on a straight line sum to 180°).","Angle CDA = 180° − 138° = 42°.","Angles in a quadrilateral sum to 360°, so x + 125 + 107 + 42 = 360.","x = 360 − 274 = 86°."]},{"id":"qd13","topic":"quad","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q14 - Square","q":"Shape ABCDE is made from square ABDE and isosceles triangle BCD, with BC = DC. The area of square ABDE is 49 cm². The perimeter of triangle BCD is 27 cm. Work out the perimeter of ABCDE.","answer":"Perimeter of ABCDE = 41 cm","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area of square ABDE = 49 cm², so each side of the square = √49 = 7 cm. This means AB = BD = DE = EA = 7 cm.","BD is the base of triangle BCD, so BD = 7 cm. Triangle BCD has perimeter 27 cm, so BC + DC = 27 − 7 = 20 cm. Since BC = DC, each = 10 cm.","The perimeter of ABCDE goes around the outside: AB + BC + CD + DE + EA (the shared side BD is internal, so it is not counted).","Perimeter = 7 + 10 + 10 + 7 + 7 = 41 cm."]},{"id":"qd14","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2023 1F Q13 - Rectangle","q":"A rectangle has one side 5 cm. An isosceles triangle has two equal sides of 8 cm and a base of 12 cm. The perimeter of the rectangle equals the perimeter of the triangle. (a) Find the area of the rectangle. The diagram also shows a cuboid with length 7 cm, height 6 cm and width w cm; its volume is 231 cm³. (b) Calculate the value of w.","answer":"(a) Area of rectangle = 45 cm²\n(b) w = 5.5 cm","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Perimeter of the triangle = 8 + 8 + 12 = 28 cm.","The rectangle's perimeter also equals 28 cm, with one side = 5 cm: 2(5 + other side) = 28, so other side = 14 − 5 = 9 cm.","(a) Area of rectangle = 5 × 9 = 45 cm².","(b) Volume of cuboid = length × height × width: 231 = 7 × 6 × w = 42w, so w = 231 ÷ 42 = 5.5 cm."]},{"id":"qd15","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2022 1F Q15 - Square","q":"Shape ABCDEFG is made from square ABDF and three identical isosceles triangles BCD, DEF and FGA. The perimeter of the square ABDF is 48 cm. The perimeter of each isosceles triangle is 30 cm. Work out the perimeter of the shape ABCDEFG.","answer":"Perimeter of ABCDEFG = 66 cm","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Perimeter of square ABDF = 48 cm, so each side = 48 ÷ 4 = 12 cm. So AB = BD = DF = FA = 12 cm.","Each triangle (e.g. BCD) is isosceles with base = a side of the square = 12 cm, and perimeter 30 cm, so the two equal sides sum to 30 − 12 = 18 cm, i.e. each equal side = 9 cm.","Triangles are attached to sides BD, DF and FA of the square (replacing each of those sides with two 9 cm sides), while side AB remains as an outer edge of the shape.","Perimeter of ABCDEFG = AB + (BC+CD) + (DE+EF) + (FG+GA) = 12 + (9+9) + (9+9) + (9+9) = 12 + 54 = 66 cm."]},{"id":"qd16","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2022 2F Q10 - Kite","q":"A kite is drawn on a centimetre grid with vertices at (1,3), (5,1), (7,3) and (5,5) (grid units in cm). On a centimetre grid, draw a rectangle that has the same area as the kite.","answer":"Area of kite = 12 cm² (diagonals 6 cm and 4 cm: ½ × 6 × 4 = 12). Any rectangle with area 12 cm² is correct, e.g. 3 cm × 4 cm, or 2 cm × 6 cm.","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["The kite's diagonals run horizontally from (1,3) to (7,3) - length 6 cm - and vertically from (5,1) to (5,5) - length 4 cm. They are perpendicular, as required for a kite.","Area of a kite = ½ × (diagonal 1) × (diagonal 2) = ½ × 6 × 4 = 12 cm².","Draw any rectangle whose sides multiply to 12, e.g. 3 cm by 4 cm."]},{"id":"qd17","topic":"quad","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q6 - Square","q":"A square has perimeter 24 cm. A shaded rectangle is made from 4 of these squares placed in a row. Work out the perimeter of the shaded rectangle.","answer":"Perimeter of shaded rectangle = 60 cm","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Perimeter of the square = 24 cm, so each side = 24 ÷ 4 = 6 cm.","Four squares placed in a row form a rectangle of length 4 × 6 = 24 cm and width 6 cm (the height of one square).","Perimeter of the rectangle = 2 × (24 + 6) = 2 × 30 = 60 cm."]},{"id":"qd18","topic":"quad","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q9 - Angles in Quadrilaterals","q":"A quadrilateral has angles 92°, x°, x° and 44°. (i) Work out the value of x. (ii) Give a reason for your answer.","answer":"(i) x = 112°\n(ii) Reason: angles in a quadrilateral sum to 360°.","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Angles in a quadrilateral sum to 360°: 92 + x + x + 44 = 360.","2x = 360 − 136 = 224, so x = 112°."]},{"id":"qd19","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2026 1F Q17 - Parallelogram","q":"A parallelogram and a trapezium both have a base of 25 cm and a perpendicular height of h cm. The trapezium's other parallel side is 11 cm. The area of the parallelogram is 175 cm². Work out the area of the trapezium as a percentage of the area of the parallelogram.","answer":"Area of trapezium as a percentage of the parallelogram = 72%","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area of parallelogram = base × height: 175 = 25 × h, so h = 7 cm.","Area of trapezium = ½ × (11 + 25) × 7 = ½ × 36 × 7 = 126 cm².","Percentage = (126 ÷ 175) × 100 = 72%."]},{"id":"qd20","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2026 2F Q14 - Rectangle","q":"A rectangular floor measures 15 m by 3.8 m. Diego buys enough tins of paint to cover the floor with one coat. Each tin covers 2.5 m² and costs 184 pesos. Diego buys the least possible number of tins. Work out the total cost of the tins.","answer":"Total cost = 4232 pesos","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area of floor = 15 × 3.8 = 57 m².","Number of tins needed = 57 ÷ 2.5 = 22.8, which rounds up to 23 tins (you can't buy part of a tin, and the floor must be fully covered).","Total cost = 23 × 184 = 4232 pesos."]},{"id":"qd21","topic":"quad","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q16 - Rectangle","q":"A wall is an L-shaped (stepped) rectangle: 120 cm wide at the top for a height of 160 cm, then it steps out by 80 cm to a total width of 200 cm for the remaining height, with a total left-hand height of 240 cm. Jim has 3 boxes of tiles with 12 tiles per box; each square tile has side 40 cm. Work out the number of tiles Jim should have left after he covers the wall with tiles.","answer":"Tiles left = 14","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Split the wall into two rectangles: the top part is 120 cm × 160 cm = 19200 cm²; the bottom part is (120+80) cm × (240−160) cm = 200 × 80 = 16000 cm².","Total wall area = 19200 + 16000 = 35200 cm².","Each tile covers 40 × 40 = 1600 cm². Tiles needed = 35200 ÷ 1600 = 22 tiles exactly.","Jim has 3 × 12 = 36 tiles in total. Tiles left = 36 − 22 = 14."]},{"id":"qd22","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2025 1F Q17 - Rectangle","q":"A stage is made of a 6 m by 8 m rectangle plus an isosceles triangle attached to one 6 m side, with the triangle's apex 3 m from that side. Yuko needs to cover the stage with varnish; each tin covers 4 m². Work out the smallest number of tins needed.","answer":"15 tins","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area of rectangle = 6 × 8 = 48 m².","Area of triangle = ½ × base × height = ½ × 6 × 3 = 9 m².","Total area = 48 + 9 = 57 m².","Tins needed = 57 ÷ 4 = 14.25, which rounds up to 15 tins (whole tins only, must cover everything)."]},{"id":"qd23","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2025 1F Q26 - Trapezium","q":"ABCD is a trapezium with one line of symmetry. Angle ADC = 60°, AD = 12 cm, DC = 47 cm. Work out the area of the trapezium, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"Area ≈ 426 cm²","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Since the trapezium has one line of symmetry, it is isosceles: AD = BC = 12 cm, and the perpendicular height h is the same on both sides.","Drop a perpendicular from A to DC: height h = AD × sin(60°) = 12 × 0.8660... = 10.392 cm. The horizontal offset from D to the foot of this perpendicular = AD × cos(60°) = 12 × 0.5 = 6 cm.","By symmetry, the same 6 cm offset occurs on the other side, so AB = DC − 2×6 = 47 − 12 = 35 cm.","Area = ½ × (AB + DC) × h = ½ × (35 + 47) × 10.392 = 41 × 10.392 = 426.07... cm² ≈ 426 cm² (3 s.f.)."]},{"id":"qd24","topic":"quad","ref":"Nov 2024 1F Q13 - Rectangle","q":"A rectangular wall measures 3.6 m by 2.1 m. Square tiles measure 0.3 m by 0.3 m, sold in boxes of 6 for £17.50 per box. Hamish wants to cover all the wall with tiles. Work out the total cost of the tiles Hamish needs.","answer":"Total cost = £245","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area of wall = 3.6 × 2.1 = 7.56 m².","Area of one tile = 0.3 × 0.3 = 0.09 m².","Number of tiles needed = 7.56 ÷ 0.09 = 84 tiles exactly.","Number of boxes = 84 ÷ 6 = 14 boxes exactly.","Total cost = 14 × £17.50 = £245."]},{"id":"qd25","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2024 2F Q23 - Trapezium","q":"A 6-sided shape ABCDEF has AF = 21 cm (bottom), CD = 15 cm (top, parallel to AF), AB = FE = 13 cm, and perpendicular height h cm. The area of the shape is 390 cm². Work out the value of h.","answer":"h = 21.7 cm (3 s.f.), i.e. 21⅔ cm","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Since CD is parallel to AF, the shape is a trapezium with parallel sides AF = 21 cm and CD = 15 cm, and height h.","Area = ½ × (AF + CD) × h: 390 = ½ × (21+15) × h = ½ × 36 × h = 18h.","h = 390 ÷ 18 = 21.666... ≈ 21.7 cm (3 s.f.)."]},{"id":"qd26","topic":"quad","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q26 - Rectangle","q":"Hexagon ABCDEF has AB = 25 cm, BC = (x+2) cm, CD = 8 cm, EF = 7 cm, AF = (x+6) cm, with right angles at A, B and F. The area of hexagon ABCDEF is 258 cm². Work out the value of x.","answer":"x = 6.4","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Place A at the origin: A(0,0), B(0,25) [since AB=25, vertical], C(x+2, 25) [BC horizontal], D(x+2, 17) [CD=8 vertical down], F(x+6, 0) [AF horizontal], E(x+6, 7) [EF=7 vertical, E above F].","Using the shoelace formula on A, B, C, D, E, F in order gives the hexagon's area as 25x + 98.","Set 25x + 98 = 258: 25x = 160, so x = 6.4.","Check: AF = x+6 = 12.4 cm, BC = x+2 = 8.4 cm - both sensible positive lengths."]},{"id":"qd27","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2023 1F Q20 - Rectangle","q":"Shaded shape AEBCD is made by removing triangle AEB from rectangle ABCD. AE = 7.2 cm, BE = 5.4 cm, BC = 6 cm, angle AEB = 90°. Work out the perimeter of the shaded shape.","answer":"Perimeter = 33.6 cm","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Triangle AEB is right-angled at E with legs 7.2 cm and 5.4 cm, so by Pythagoras: AB = √(7.2² + 5.4²) = √(51.84+29.16) = √81 = 9 cm.","AB is a side of rectangle ABCD, so AB = DC = 9 cm, and BC = AD = 6 cm (given).","The shaded shape's boundary is A→E→B→C→D→A, so perimeter = AE + EB + BC + CD + DA = 7.2 + 5.4 + 6 + 9 + 6 = 33.6 cm."]},{"id":"qd28","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2023 1F Q19 - Trapezium","q":"ABCD is a trapezium with BC parallel to AD. Angle BAD = (4x−27)°, angle ABC = (3x+46)°, angle ADC = (3x+10)°. Find the size of the largest angle inside the trapezium.","answer":"Largest angle = 115°","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Since BC is parallel to AD, angles ABC and BAD are co-interior angles on the transversal AB, so they sum to 180°.","(3x+46) + (4x−27) = 180 → 7x + 19 = 180 → 7x = 161 → x = 23.","Angle BAD = 4(23)−27 = 65°. Angle ABC = 3(23)+46 = 115°. Angle ADC = 3(23)+10 = 79°.","Angle BCD = 360 − (65+115+79) = 101° (or using co-interior angles on CD: 180−79 = 101°, which checks out).","The largest of 65°, 115°, 79°, 101° is 115°."]},{"id":"qd29","topic":"quad","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q15 - Rectangle","q":"A stage floor plan is a triangle on top of a rectangle: rectangle 4.8 m by 3 m, with an isosceles triangle on top (base 4.8 m, height 2.5 m). Paint covers 1.8 m² per tin, costing $16.40 per tin, bought only in full tins. The stage manager has $190. Does the stage manager have enough money to buy enough tins to paint all of the floor?","answer":"No - 12 tins are needed, costing $196.80, which is more than the $190 available (short by $6.80).","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area of rectangle = 4.8 × 3 = 14.4 m². Area of triangle = ½ × 4.8 × 2.5 = 6 m².","Total area = 14.4 + 6 = 20.4 m².","Tins needed = 20.4 ÷ 1.8 = 11.33..., which rounds up to 12 whole tins.","Cost = 12 × $16.40 = $196.80, which is more than the $190 available, so no - there isn't enough money."]},{"id":"qd30","topic":"quad","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q19 - Rectangle","q":"Rectangle ABCD has AB = 24 cm, AD = (5x−1) cm and BC = (3x+7.4) cm. Work out the perimeter of the rectangle.","answer":"Perimeter = 88 cm","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["In a rectangle, opposite sides are equal, so AD = BC: 5x−1 = 3x+7.4.","2x = 8.4, so x = 4.2.","AD = 5(4.2)−1 = 20 cm (check: BC = 3(4.2)+7.4 = 20 cm ✓).","Perimeter = 2 × (AB + AD) = 2 × (24+20) = 2 × 44 = 88 cm."]},{"id":"qd31","topic":"quad","ref":"June 2022 2F Q21 - Trapezium","q":"An 8-sided shape ABCDEFGH has HG = 28 cm, FG = 12 cm, AB = EF = 5 cm, height 20 cm, with CD parallel to HG. The area of the shape is 434 cm². Find the length of CD.","answer":"CD = 6.5 cm","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["With right angles at H and G, and by symmetry A is also 12 cm above H (matching FG=12): H(0,0), G(28,0), A(0,12), F(28,12), B(5,12) [AB=5], E(23,12) [EF=5].","Split the shape into a bottom rectangle H,G,F,A (28 × 12 = 336 cm²) and a top trapezium sitting on BE with parallel sides BE and CD, height 20−12 = 8 cm.","BE = 23 − 5 = 18 cm. Top trapezium area = ½ × (18+CD) × 8 = 72 + 4×CD.","Total area: 336 + 72 + 4×CD = 434 → 4×CD = 26 → CD = 6.5 cm."]},{"id":"qd32","topic":"quad","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q13 - Trapezium","q":"A classroom wall is a right trapezium: the two parallel (vertical) sides are 2.5 m and 3.5 m, with a 6.5 m horizontal side between their bases. Dion wants to paint the wall completely twice; each tin covers 12 m², and he can only buy whole tins. Work out the least number of tins of paint Dion needs to buy.","answer":"4 tins","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["The wall is a trapezium with parallel sides 2.5 m and 3.5 m, and the perpendicular distance between them (the 'height' in the area formula) is the 6.5 m base.","Area = ½ × (2.5+3.5) × 6.5 = ½ × 6 × 6.5 = 19.5 m².","Painting twice means covering 19.5 × 2 = 39 m² in total.","Tins needed = 39 ÷ 12 = 3.25, which rounds up to 4 whole tins."]},{"id":"ci1","topic":"circles","ref":"June 2025 2F Q15 - Area and Circumference","q":"A circle has radius 16 cm. Calculate the circumference of the circle, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"Circumference ≈ 101 cm","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Circumference = 2πr = 2 × π × 16 = 32π = 100.53...","Rounded to 3 s.f.: 101 cm."]},{"id":"ci2","topic":"circles","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q16 - Area and Circumference","q":"A circle has radius 9 cm. Work out the area of the circle, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"Area ≈ 254 cm²","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area = πr² = π × 9² = 81π = 254.47...","Rounded to 3 s.f.: 254 cm²."]},{"id":"ci3","topic":"circles","ref":"June 2024 2F Q9 - Area and Circumference","q":"A circle has a radius of 9 cm. Calculate the area of the circle, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"Area ≈ 254 cm²","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area = πr² = π × 9² = 81π = 254.47...","Rounded to 3 s.f.: 254 cm²."]},{"id":"ci4","topic":"circles","ref":"June 2023 2F Q12 - Area and Circumference","q":"A circle has radius 8.5 cm. Work out the circumference of the circle, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"Circumference ≈ 53.4 cm","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Circumference = 2πr = 2 × π × 8.5 = 17π = 53.407...","Rounded to 3 s.f.: 53.4 cm."]},{"id":"ci5","topic":"circles","ref":"June 2022 2F Q7 - Area and Circumference","q":"A circle has radius 6.5 cm. Calculate the circumference of the circle, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"Circumference ≈ 40.8 cm","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Circumference = 2πr = 2 × π × 6.5 = 13π = 40.841...","Rounded to 3 s.f.: 40.8 cm."]},{"id":"ci6","topic":"circles","ref":"June 2023 2F Q23 - Circles (Tangents)","q":"A and C are points on a circle, centre O. DA is the tangent to the circle at A and DC is the tangent at C. Angle ADC = 48°. Work out the size of reflex angle AOC.","answer":"Reflex angle AOC = 228°","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["A tangent meets a radius at 90°, so angle OAD = angle OCD = 90°.","Angles in quadrilateral OADC sum to 360°: angle AOC (non-reflex) + 90 + 90 + 48 = 360, so angle AOC = 360 − 228 = 132°.","The reflex angle AOC = 360° − 132° = 228°."]},{"id":"ci7","topic":"circles","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q10 - Area and Circumference","q":"A circle has a diameter of 14 cm. Calculate the area of the circle, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"Area ≈ 154 cm²","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Radius = diameter ÷ 2 = 7 cm.","Area = πr² = π × 7² = 49π = 153.94...","Rounded to 3 s.f.: 154 cm²."]},{"id":"ci8","topic":"circles","ref":"June 2026 1F Q28 - Shaded Regions","q":"Shaded shape ABCDEO is made from a semicircle BCD and two identical right-angled triangles ABO and EDO. BD is the diameter of the semicircle and O is its midpoint. Angle ABO = angle EDO = 90°, AO = EO = 15 cm. The area of semicircle BCD is 227 cm². Work out the perimeter of the shaded shape, correct to 1 decimal place.","answer":"Perimeter ≈ 85.7 cm","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Semicircle area = ½πr² = 227, so r² = 2×227/π = 144.51, giving r = 12.02 cm.","In right-angled triangle ABO (right angle at B), BO = r (a radius) and AO = 15 cm (hypotenuse). By Pythagoras, AB = √(15² − r²) = √(225 − 144.51) = √80.49 = 8.972 cm. The same applies to DE.","The semicircular arc length BCD = πr = π × 12.02 = 37.76 cm.","Perimeter = AB + arc(BCD) + DE + EO + OA = 8.972 + 37.76 + 8.972 + 15 + 15 = 85.7 cm (1 d.p.)."]},{"id":"ci9","topic":"circles","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q23 - Circles","q":"A large circle with centre O contains 3 identical small circles, each touching two others, with centres A, O and B on a straight line. The circumference of the large circle is 160 cm. Work out the area of one small circle, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"Area of one small circle ≈ 226 cm²","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Three small circles placed in a row span the full diameter of the large circle, so the large circle's diameter = 3 × (small circle's diameter), i.e. large radius = 3 × small radius.","Large circumference = 160 = 2πR, so R = 160/(2π) = 25.465 cm.","Small radius r = R/3 = 25.465/3 = 8.488 cm.","Area of one small circle = πr² = π × 8.488² = 226.35... ≈ 226 cm² (3 s.f.)."]},{"id":"ci10","topic":"circles","ref":"Nov 2023 1F Q13 - Area and Circumference","q":"A wheel on a tractor has a diameter of 160 cm. The tractor travels 1750 metres. Work out the number of complete turns made by the wheel.","answer":"348 complete turns","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Circumference of wheel = π × diameter = π × 160 = 502.65 cm = 5.0265 m.","Number of turns = distance ÷ circumference = 1750 ÷ 5.0265 = 348.19...","Only complete turns count, so round down: 348 complete turns."]},{"id":"ci11","topic":"circles","ref":"Nov 2023 1F Q19 - Shaded Regions","q":"A shaded shape is made from three identical semicircles X, Y and Z. ABCDE is a straight line. AC is the diameter of semicircle X (centre B), BD is the diameter of semicircle Y (centre C), CE is the diameter of semicircle Z (centre D). AC = BD = CE = 20 cm. Work out the perimeter of the shaded shape, correct to the nearest whole number.","answer":"Perimeter ≈ 94 cm","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Each semicircle has diameter 20 cm, so radius 10 cm. The perimeter of the S-shaped figure is made up of exactly the 3 semicircular arcs (the diameters are all internal, shared between adjacent semicircles).","One semicircular arc length = πr = π × 10 = 10π cm.","Perimeter = 3 × 10π = 30π = 94.25 cm ≈ 94 cm (nearest whole number)."]},{"id":"ci12","topic":"circles","ref":"June 2022 1F Q25 - Circles","q":"Circle C1 has centre (-1, 3) and radius 13 cm. Circle C2 has centre (7, 18) and radius 6 cm (1 cm = 1 unit on each axis). (a) Work out the distance between the centre of C1 and the centre of C2. (b) Explain why circle C1 intersects circle C2.","answer":"(a) Distance = 17 cm\n(b) C1 intersects C2 because the distance between centres (17) is less than the sum of the radii (13+6=19) but more than the difference of the radii (13−6=7), i.e. 7 < 17 < 19.","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Use Pythagoras on the horizontal and vertical differences: Δx = 7−(−1)=8, Δy=18−3=15. Distance = √(8²+15²) = √(64+225) = √289 = 17.","(b) Sum of radii = 13+6 = 19; difference of radii = 13−6 = 7. Since 7 < 17 < 19, the circles must overlap at two points - neither one contains the other, and they are not too far apart to touch."]},{"id":"ci13","topic":"circles","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q22 - Shaded Regions","q":"A shape is made from square ABCD and 4 identical semicircles, with AB, BC, CD and DA as diameters. The area of the square is 36 cm². Calculate the total area of the shape, correct to 1 decimal place.","answer":"Total area ≈ 92.5 cm²","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area of square = 36 cm², so each side = √36 = 6 cm. Each semicircle has diameter 6 cm, so radius 3 cm.","Area of one semicircle = ½πr² = ½π(3²) = 4.5π cm². There are 4 semicircles: 4 × 4.5π = 18π cm².","Total area = square + 4 semicircles = 36 + 18π = 36 + 56.549 = 92.5 cm² (1 d.p.)."]},{"id":"ci14","topic":"circles","ref":"Nov 2025 1H Q15 - Sectors","q":"AOB is a sector of a circle with centre O and radius 12 cm. Angle AOB = 75°. Work out the area of the sector, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"Area ≈ 94.2 cm²","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area of sector = (θ/360) × πr² = (75/360) × π × 12² = (75/360) × 144π = 30π.","30π = 94.2478... ≈ 94.2 cm² (3 s.f.)."]},{"id":"ci15","topic":"circles","ref":"June 2025 1H Q11 - Sectors","q":"OABC is a sector of a circle, centre O. Angle AOC = 140°, OA = OC = 16 cm. Calculate the area of the sector, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"Area ≈ 313 cm²","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area of sector = (θ/360) × πr² = (140/360) × π × 16² = (140/360) × 256π.","(140/360) × 256 = 99.556, so area = 99.556π = 312.76... ≈ 313 cm² (3 s.f.)."]},{"id":"ci16","topic":"circles","ref":"June 2026 2H Q15 - Sectors","q":"The diagram shows a sector OABC of a circle, centre O. OA = OC = r cm, angle AOC = 80°. The area of the sector OABC is 32π cm². Work out the perimeter of the sector OABC, correct to 1 decimal place.","answer":"Perimeter ≈ 40.8 cm","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Area of sector = (θ/360)πr²: 32π = (80/360)πr², so r² = 32 × (360/80) = 32 × 4.5 = 144, giving r = 12 cm.","Arc length = (θ/360) × 2πr = (80/360) × 2π(12) = (80/360) × 24π = 16.755 cm.","Perimeter = 2r + arc length = 2(12) + 16.755 = 24 + 16.755 = 40.755 ≈ 40.8 cm (1 d.p.)."]},{"id":"ci17","topic":"circles","ref":"June 2022 2H Q20 - Shaded Regions","q":"Four identical circles are drawn inside a square, each circle touching two other circles and two sides of the square. The region inside the square that is outside the circles (shaded) has total area 40 cm². Work out the perimeter of the square, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"Perimeter ≈ 54.6 cm","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["With circles in a 2×2 arrangement, the square's side = 4r (two circle-diameters across), where r is each circle's radius.","Square area = (4r)² = 16r². Total circle area = 4πr².","Shaded area = square − circles: 16r² − 4πr² = 40, so r²(16−4π) = 40, giving r² = 40/(16−4π) = 11.651, so r = 3.413 cm.","Square side = 4r = 13.654 cm. Perimeter = 4 × 13.654 = 54.614 ≈ 54.6 cm (3 s.f.)."]},{"id":"ci18","topic":"circles","ref":"Nov 2024 1H Q16 - Sectors","q":"OAPB is a sector of a circle, centre O. Angle AOB = 50°. The area of triangle OAB is 120 cm². Work out the area of the sector OAPB, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"Area of sector ≈ 137 cm²","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Triangle OAB is isosceles with OA = OB = r. Area of triangle = ½ r² sin(50°) = 120, so r² = 240/sin(50°) = 240/0.76604 = 313.31.","Area of sector = (θ/360)πr² = (50/360) × π × 313.31 = 0.13889 × 984.33 = 136.71.","Rounded to 3 s.f.: 137 cm²."]},{"id":"ci19","topic":"circles","ref":"Nov 2024 1H Q25 - Circles","q":"The diagram shows an equilateral triangle ABC with an inscribed circle, centre O, radius x cm. AB, BC and CA are tangents to the circle. The total shaded area (triangle minus circle) is nx² cm². Find the value of n, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"n ≈ 2.05","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["For an equilateral triangle, the inradius x relates to the side length a by x = a/(2√3), so a = 2√3 x.","Area of the equilateral triangle = (√3/4)a² = (√3/4)(2√3x)² = (√3/4)(12x²) = 3√3 x².","Shaded area = triangle − circle = 3√3x² − πx² = (3√3 − π)x².","n = 3√3 − π = 5.19615 − 3.14159 = 2.0546 ≈ 2.05 (3 s.f.)."]}];